# AI Research Orchestrator — Manifest

**Purpose:** Client-only PWA for agentic biomedical literature research: PubMed/NCBI, arXiv, multi-provider AI (Gemini / OpenAI / Anthropic / Ollama) or deterministic heuristic fallback, local Knowledge Base, and export — no application backend for user data.

**Stack:** React 19, TypeScript strict, Vite 8, Redux Toolkit, Dexie 4 + dexie-react-hooks (IndexedDB), Tailwind CSS v4, lazy provider SDKs, Marked/DOMPurify, jsPDF, **Recharts only**, Framer Motion, cmdk, Vitest + Testing Library, Playwright E2E (blocking Chromium + blocking Firefox/WebKit/mobile Chrome). Inference: `live | heuristic` (`src/services/nonAi/`, ADR 0007/0009).

**Architecture:** Browser talks directly to the selected AI provider + NCBI E-utilities (+ arXiv); AES-GCM keys via `apiKeyService`; Redux is the single source of truth; Context only hydrates/composes (`SettingsProvider`, KB) — never duplicate the same settings/UI flags. Synthesis trust: corpus-/claim-supported vs unverified narrative draft (ADR 0018).

**Conventions:** EN+DE in `src/i18n/translations.ts`; WCAG-oriented (ARIA, keyboard); new persistent data → Dexie schema in `databaseService`; Node **≥22**; `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. Before commit: `typecheck` + `lint`; for core orchestration / Knowledge Base / `src/services` flows also run `pnpm run test:coverage` (or read the blocking CI coverage job). Prefer scoped Vitest/Playwright locally for unrelated UI edits; full coverage/E2E from CI. English-only new repo content (rule `010`).

**PR / CI gates:** Rules `011`/`013` — always `@deepsourcebot review`; resolve bot threads; CodeRabbit rate-limit loop (bounded). Blocking checks + PR-only `cancel-in-progress`: `docs/ci-branch-governance.md` + `docs/project-facts.json` (drift-gated). Live ruleset: `mainrules`.

**Modular rules:** `.cursor/rules/` — `001–099` Security/PR gates, `100–199` APIs, `200–299` Architecture, `300–399` UI, `800–899` QA/Workflows; details in `000-cursor-rules.mdc`.

**Canonical:** `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `README.md`, `docs/ci-branch-governance.md`, `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`.
